␀␀␀␀current␀temperature_2m␀␀apparent_temperature␀␀␀␀weather_code␀␀␀␀wind_speed_10m␀␀is_day␀␀daily␀␀␀temperature_2m_max␀␀temperature_2m_min␀␀precipitation_probability_max␀␀␀sunrise␀sunset␀␀hourly␀␀precipitation_probability␀␀␀https://geocoding-api.open-meteo.com/v1/search?count=1&language=en&name=␀␀␀␀results␀latitude␀␀␀␀longitude␀␀␀YouTube channels need the YouTube Data API key.␀Add at least one YouTube or Twitch channel.␀pin2␀␀␀␀nopin␀␀␀PINs don't match␀␀␀␀Type the same PIN in both boxes. Nothing was saved.␀PIN too short␀␀␀Use at least 4 characters. Nothing was saved.␀␀␀	␀␀␀Missing details␀Check the network settings␀␀A fixed IP needs a valid IP and gateway, e.g. 192.168.1.250 and 192.168.1.1.␀␀␀␀pref␀␀␀␀rm␀␀No Wi-Fi network␀␀␀␀Too many networks␀␀␀You can save up to 5. Remove one first.␀Add at least one Wi-Fi network.␀http␀␀␀␀sumHour␀wxtown␀␀Town not found␀␀Couldn't find "␀". Try a nearby town or add the country, e.g. "Paisley, UK".␀␀␀␀spsecret␀␀␀␀nightStart␀␀nightEnd␀␀␀␀Saved &#10003;␀␀The board is restarting and will join whichever saved network is in range.␀␀Saved!␀␀Restarting...␀␀␀Basic ␀␀https://accounts.spotify.com/api/token␀␀Can't reach Spotify␀Content-Type␀␀␀␀application/x-www-form-urlencoded␀␀␀error_description␀␀␀access_token␀␀␀␀expires_in␀␀refresh_token␀␀␀grant_type=refresh_token&refresh_token=␀https://api.spotify.com/v1␀␀/me/player?market=from_token␀␀␀␀Not connected␀␀␀Spotify error ␀␀is_playing␀␀progress_ms␀volume_percent␀␀item␀␀␀␀duration_ms␀artists␀show␀␀␀␀album␀␀␀images␀␀width␀␀␀/me/player/pause␀␀␀␀/me/player/play␀PUT␀/me/player/next␀POST␀␀␀␀/me/player/previous␀/me/player/volume?volume_percent=␀␀␀Volume ␀Needs Spotify Premium␀␀␀No active device␀␀␀␀code=␀␀␀No code found in what you pasted␀␀␀␀grant_type=authorization_code&code=␀Spotify connected &#10003;␀␀Long-press the board's screen and choose Spotify.␀␀␀Couldn't connect Spotify␀␀␀␀. Codes only work once and expire after a few minutes &ndash; open the Spotify link again and paste the new address.␀␀␀␀Spotify not connected␀␀␀Spotify said: ␀␀<h1>Spotify connected &#10003;</h1><p>Long-press the board's screen and choose Spotify.</p><a href='/'>Go to the dashboard</a></div></body></html>␀␀. Press Connect Spotify on the settings page to try again.␀␀client_id=␀␀Twitch: add your Client ID and Secret in settings␀␀␀&client_secret=␀&grant_type=client_credentials␀␀https://id.twitch.tv/oauth2/token␀␀␀Twitch: Client ID or Secret is wrong␀␀␀␀Twitch: can't sign in (␀login=␀␀users?␀␀login␀␀␀display_name␀␀␀␀profile_image_url␀␀␀created_at␀␀Twitch channel not found␀␀␀␀Twitch error ␀␀␀channels/followers?first=1&broadcaster_id=␀␀total␀␀␀user_id=␀␀␀␀streams?␀␀␀␀user_id␀viewer_count␀␀␀␀started_at␀␀game_name␀␀␀thumbnail_url␀␀␀{width}␀320␀{height}␀␀␀␀180␀update check␀␀␀␀Spotify command␀channel counts␀␀live streams␀␀␀␀profile pictures␀␀␀␀latest videos␀␀␀comments␀␀␀␀new video tracker␀␀␀typical views␀␀␀weather␀recent uploads␀␀phone notifications␀closing connections␀idle␀␀␀␀NOT found␀␀␀Touch controller %s
␀␀␀␀Motion sensor NOT found␀Motion sensor found at 0x%02X
␀␀Setup mode␀␀Scanning Wi-Fi...␀␀␀[␀␀␀,[␀␀i␀␀␀days␀␀␀␀kind␀␀␀␀%lld␀␀␀␀all-channels␀␀␀␀Content-Disposition␀attachment; filename="subcounter-␀␀␀.csv"␀␀␀text/csv␀␀␀␀channel,time_utc,subscribers
␀␀␀%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ␀␀",␀␀<a href='#firmware'>Firmware</a>␀␀␀␀(saved â€” leave blank to keep)␀AIzaâ€¦␀ open␀␀␀ (saved &#10003;)␀␀␀ (needed for Twitch channels)␀␀␀ minute␀ minutes␀␀␀␀ required␀␀␀Password␀␀␀␀New PIN␀Choose a PIN (4â€“12 characters)␀␀␀␀Leave blank to keep the current PIN␀e.g. 4 digits␀␀␀<h1>&#9654; SubCounter settings</h1><p>Saved on the board only. v13.9␀␀␀ &middot; <a href='/'>&larr; Dashboard</a>␀␀</p><nav class='jump'><a href='#channels'>YouTube</a><a href='#twitch'>Twitch</a><a href='#display'>Display</a><a href='#alerts'>Alerts</a><a href='#phone'>Phone</a><a href='#weather'>Weather</a><a href='#spotify'>Spotify</a><a href='#motion'>Motion</a><a href='#wifi'>Wi-Fi</a><a href='#updates'>Updates</a><a href='#security'>Security</a>␀␀␀␀</nav>␀␀<div style='background:#3a1210;border:1px solid #e62117;border-radius:10px;padding:12px;margin-bottom:8px;font-size:14px'><b>Couldn't connect to Wi-Fi:</b><br>␀<form method='POST' action='/save'>␀<label>YouTube channels (one per line)</label>␀␀<textarea name='channels' autocapitalize='off' autocorrect='off' spellcheck='false' placeholder='@yourchannel&#10;@mkbhd&#10;@veritasium'>␀␀</textarea>␀<small>@handles, UCâ€¦ channel IDs or channel links. Put your own channel first â€“ it's highlighted and shown on the night clock.</small>␀␀<label>YouTube Data API key</label>␀<input name='apikey' autocapitalize='off' autocomplete='off' placeholder='␀␀'><small>Only needed if you follow YouTube channels.</small>␀␀␀␀<label>Twitch channels (just the name, one per line)</label>␀␀␀␀<textarea name='twch' autocapitalize='off' autocorrect='off' spellcheck='false' style='min-height:90px' placeholder='shroud&#10;pokimane'>␀␀<small>Type the name as it appears in their Twitch address (twitch.tv/<b>name</b>). Pasting the full link works too. YouTube and Twitch together: up to 10 channels.</small>␀␀␀␀<details␀␀␀␀><summary>Twitch app details␀␀␀␀<small>Create a free app at <a href='https://dev.twitch.tv/console/apps' target='_blank'>dev.twitch.tv/console</a>: Register Your Application &rarr; any unique name &rarr; OAuth Redirect URL <code>https://localhost</code> (any https address works, it isn't used) &rarr; Category: Other &rarr; Client type: Confidential &rarr; Create &rarr; Manage &rarr; copy the Client ID and a <b>New Secret</b>. Your Twitch account needs two-factor sign-in turned on.</small>␀␀␀<label>Client ID</label><input name='twid' autocapitalize='off' autocomplete='off' value='␀␀<label>Client Secret</label><input name='twsec' type='text' class='secret' autocapitalize='off' autocomplete='off' spellcheck='false' placeholder='␀Display␀display␀<label>Colour theme</label><select name='theme'>␀␀␀␀</select><small>Accent colour on the board and the dashboard.</small>␀␀␀<label>Screen brightness: <b id='bv'>␀␀␀%</b></label><input type='range' name='bright' min='10' max='100' step='5' value='␀␀' oninput="bv.textContent=this.value+'%'" style='padding:0'>␀␀␀␀<label>Night clock brightness: <b id='nv'>␀␀%</b></label><input type='range' name='nbright' min='1' max='40' value='␀␀␀␀' oninput="nv.textContent=this.value+'%'" style='padding:0'>␀␀␀␀Switch channels automatically every 10 seconds␀␀Estimated live counts between YouTube's rounded steps (â€œest.â€)␀␀Show estimated earnings on the dashboard (YouTube)␀␀Â£ pounds␀␀␀$ dollars␀␀␀â‚¬ euros␀␀␀<div class='row'><select name='earnCur'>␀␀␀␀</select><input name='earnLo' type='number' step='0.01' min='0' value='␀' title='Low'><span>to</span><input name='earnHi' type='number' step='0.01' min='0' value='␀' title='High'></div>␀␀␀<small>Earnings per 1,000 views, low to high. YouTube doesn't publish what channels earn, so the dashboard shows a range worked out from views (like Social Blade). Typical is about 0.20 to 3.50; narrow it if you know a channel's real rate.</small>␀<label>Show the big clock after this long without use</label><select name='idleclk'>␀␀␀␀Never␀␀␀</select><small>Touch, press BOOT or pick the board up to go back.</small>␀␀<label>Night clock (dims and shows the time)</label><div class='row'>␀␀␀<span>to</span>␀<label>Subscriber race</label><div class='row'>␀<span>vs</span>␀<div id='rpv' class='rpv'></div><script>const PI={yt:"<svg width='20' height='14' viewBox='0 0 20 14'><rect width='20' height='14' rx='4' fill='#ff0033'/><path d='M8 4v6l5-3z' fill='#fff'/></svg>",tw:"<svg width='16' height='16' viewBox='0 0 16 16'><path d='M2 1h13v9l-4 4H8l-2 2H4v-2H1V4z' fill='#9146ff'/><path d='M7 4h1.5v4H7zM10.5 4H12v4h-1.5z' fill='#fff'/></svg>"};function racePv(){const f=n=>{const o=document.querySelector("select[name="+n+"]").selectedOptions[0];return o&&o.value!='-1'?'<span>'+PI[o.dataset.p]+' '+o.textContent.replace(/</g,'&lt;')+'</span>':'<span style=\'color:#777\'>None</span>'};document.getElementById('rpv').innerHTML=f('raceA')+'<em>vs</em>'+f('raceB')}racePv()</script>␀<small>Swipe down twice from the main count to see it.</small>␀␀Alerts␀␀alerts␀␀Confetti for milestones (bigger milestones, bigger party)␀␀␀Alert when a channel goes live (and switch to it)␀␀␀<label>Daily summary on the board (a monthly recap on the 1st)</label>␀␀<small>Shows for 10 minutes at this time; touch to close it. It's also on the dashboard all day, and on the board any time: long-press &rarr; swipe left &rarr; <b>Summary</b>.</small>␀<small>New-subscriber, overtake and record alerts are always on. Alerts are skipped at night, when the board is face-down, and while Spotify is playing.</small>␀␀␀␀Phone notifications␀phone␀␀␀<small>Get alerts on your phone with the free <b>ntfy</b> app (iPhone and Android, no account needed). Install it, tap <b>+</b>, subscribe to the topic below, then save.</small>␀␀␀subcounter-␀<label>ntfy topic (blank = off)</label><input name='ntfy' autocapitalize='off' autocomplete='off' spellcheck='false' value='␀␀␀␀' placeholder='e.g. ␀␀␀␀<small>Anyone who knows the topic name can read it, so make it hard to guess.</small>␀␀␀<details><summary>Own ntfy server (advanced)</summary><label>Server address</label><input name='ntfysrv' autocapitalize='off' value='␀␀␀'></details>␀␀␀␀<button type='submit' class='b2' formaction='/ntfy/test' formnovalidate>Send a test notification</button>␀␀␀<label>Town or city</label><input name='wxtown' value='␀' placeholder='e.g. Glasgow'>␀␀␀<small>Long-press the board's screen and pick Weather. Forecasts from Open-Meteo.</small>␀␀␀spotify␀<p class='ok'>Connected &#10003;</p>␀␀␀␀><summary>Spotify app details (one-time setup, needs Premium)</summary>␀<small>Put the relay page on GitHub Pages (or any https address you own), then at <b>developer.spotify.com/dashboard</b> &rarr; Create app &rarr; add that https address as the Redirect URI &rarr; tick <b>Web API</b> &rarr; Save. Copy the Client ID, Client secret and the same Redirect URI here, and save.</small>␀␀␀␀<label>Redirect URI (exactly as entered at Spotify)</label><input name='spredir' value='␀␀␀␀' autocapitalize='off' placeholder='https://yourname.github.io/spotify-callback/'>␀␀<label>Client ID</label><input name='spid' value='␀␀' autocapitalize='off' autocomplete='off'>␀␀<label>Client secret</label><input name='spsecret' type='text' class='secret' autocapitalize='off' autocomplete='off' spellcheck='false' placeholder='␀␀<a class='btnlink' href='␀␀␀'>Connect Spotify</a><small>Press Agree on Spotify's page and you'll be brought straight back here.</small><details><summary>The relay page showed a code instead?</summary><label>Paste the code or that page's full address</label><input name='url' placeholder='code or full address' autocapitalize='off'><button type='submit' class='b2' formaction='/spotify/code' formnovalidate>Use this code</button></details>␀␀<button type='submit' class='b2' formaction='/spotify/disconnect' formnovalidate>Disconnect Spotify</button>␀␀␀␀<small>Save the app details first; a <b>Connect Spotify</b> button then appears here.</small>␀␀␀Motion␀␀motion␀␀<small style='color:#e62117'>Motion sensor not detected.</small>␀␀␀␀Shake to refresh␀␀␀␀Face-down turns the screen off␀␀Stand it on its side for a tall leaderboard␀Tall leaderboard is upside down? Tick to flip it␀␀␀␀Double-tap the desk for the next channel␀␀␀␀<label>Desk tap sensitivity</label><select name='tapsens'>␀␀Low (firm knocks)␀␀␀Medium␀␀High (light taps)␀␀␀<label>Calibration</label><small>Put the board in the position you normally use it (on its stand or flat), then press:</small><button type='submit' class='b2' formaction='/calibrate' formnovalidate>Set this as the normal position</button>␀␀edit␀␀␀␀Wi-Fi networks␀␀wifi␀␀␀␀<small>The board joins your <b>Preferred</b> network when it's in range, otherwise the strongest saved one. <b>Connect now</b> switches straight away.</small><div class='st' style='margin:10px 0'>␀␀␀␀<label style='margin:4px 0 0'><input type='radio' name='pref' value='-1' style='width:auto'␀<div class='saved'><b>␀␀</b>␀␀␀␀<span style='color:#30d158'>connected</span>␀␀␀␀<button type='submit' formaction='/wifi/connect?n=␀␀' formnovalidate class='mini'>Connect now</button>␀␀<span>fixed IP</span>␀␀␀<label style='margin:0'><input type='radio' name='pref' value='␀' style='width:auto'␀␀␀␀> Preferred</label>␀<a href='/settings?edit=␀␀␀␀#wifi'>Edit</a>␀<label style='margin:0'><input type='checkbox' name='rm␀' value='1' style='width:auto'> Remove</label></div>␀␀␀␀> No preference (strongest signal wins)</label>␀<label>␀Editing: ␀␀␀Add another network (e.g. home)␀Wi-Fi network␀␀␀<button type='button' id='scanBtn' onclick='scan()' class='b2' style='margin-top:6px'>&#128246; Scan for networks</button>␀␀<div id='nets' style='margin:8px 0'></div>␀␀<input id='s' name='ssid' value='␀␀␀' placeholder='Network name (tap one above, or type it)'␀␀␀␀<small>Leave blank if you're not adding a network.</small>␀␀<label>Wi-Fi password</label>␀␀␀<input id='pw' name='pass' type='password' autocomplete='off' autocapitalize='off' placeholder='␀␀␀␀'><small><label style='display:inline;margin:0'><input type='checkbox' style='width:auto' onclick="document.getElementById('pw').type=this.checked?'text':'password'"> Show password</label></small>␀␀␀␀<label>Username (only for work Wi-Fi that asks for one)</label>␀<input name='user' value='␀␀' autocapitalize='off' placeholder='Leave blank for normal Wi-Fi'>␀␀><summary>Advanced settings for this network</summary>␀␀Compatibility mode (Wi-Fi 4 instead of Wi-Fi 6)␀<label>Fixed IP address (blank = automatic)</label>␀<input name='ip' value='␀␀␀␀' placeholder='e.g. 192.168.1.250' inputmode='decimal'>␀<label>Gateway (router) address</label>␀<input name='gw' value='␀␀␀␀' placeholder='e.g. 192.168.1.1' inputmode='decimal'>␀␀␀<label>Subnet mask</label>␀␀<input name='mask' value='␀␀' placeholder='255.255.255.0' inputmode='decimal'>␀␀<label>DNS server</label>␀␀␀<input name='dns' value='␀␀␀' placeholder='e.g. 8.8.8.8' inputmode='decimal'>␀␀␀<small>If this one doesn't answer, the board also tries 8.8.8.8.</small>␀␀␀␀Updates␀updates␀Check for updates at start-up (offers to install on the QR screen)␀␀Install new versions from GitHub automatically (at 3 am)␀␀␀␀<small>Either way the board checks once a day and shows when a new version is out; install it from the <a href='/update'>Update page</a>.</small>␀␀␀<details><summary>Update source (advanced)</summary><label>Address of the builds folder</label><input name='updurl' autocapitalize='off' value='␀␀␀␀'><small>Only change this if you build your own copy (a fork) on GitHub.</small></details>␀␀Security␀␀␀␀security␀␀␀␀<p class='ok'>PIN is on &#10003;</p>␀␀␀␀<small>No PIN set: anyone on your Wi-Fi can open this page and change things.</small>␀␀␀</label><input name='pin' type='password' inputmode='numeric' autocomplete='new-password' maxlength='12' placeholder='␀␀<label>Type it again</label><input name='pin2' type='password' inputmode='numeric' autocomplete='new-password' maxlength='12'>␀␀Remove the PIN␀␀<small>After you save, your browser asks for it whenever you open Settings or Update: user name <b>admin</b>, password = your PIN. The dashboard stays open to view. Forgotten it? Hold BOOT for 3 seconds: setup mode doesn't ask for it, so you can change it there.</small>␀␀<div class='savebar'><button type='submit'>Save &amp; restart</button></div>␀␀␀␀</form>␀Firmware␀␀␀␀firmware␀␀␀␀<p style='margin:0'>Running <b>v13.9</b> &middot; <a href='/update'>&#11014; Update</a>␀ &middot; <b style='color:#30d158'>v␀␀␀␀ available</b>␀␀Backup &amp; restore␀␀␀␀backup␀␀<small>Save all your settings to a file, e.g. before a full re-flash or to set up a second board. History and records stay on the board.</small><a class='btnlink' style='background:#2a2a2e' href='/backup'>&#11015; Download settings</a><small><a href='/backup?secrets=1'>Download including passwords, keys and sign-ins</a> â€“ keep that file private.</small><label>Restore from a file</label><input type='file' id='rf' accept='.json'><button type='button' class='b2' onclick='restore()'>Restore &amp; restart</button><small id='rm'></small><script>function restore(){const f=document.getElementById('rf').files[0],m=document.getElementById('rm');if(!f){m.textContent='Choose the .json file first.';return}f.text().then(t=>fetch('/restore',{method:'POST',headers:{'Content-Type':'application/json'},body:t})).then(r=>r.text()).then(t=>{m.textContent=t;setTimeout(()=>location.href='/',12000)}).catch(()=>m.textContent='Restore failed.')}</script>␀␀␀␀<small style='margin-top:16px'>Board Wi-Fi MAC address: ␀␀␀␀</small></div>␀␀<script>scan()</script>␀"v␀␀If-None-Match␀␀␀ETag␀␀␀␀no-cache␀␀␀␀Content-Encoding␀␀␀␀gzip␀␀␀␀-with-keys␀␀secrets␀with_secrets␀␀␀␀nvs␀%02x␀␀␀␀attachment; filename="subcounter-settings␀␀␀.json"␀␀updatedAgo␀␀err␀ver␀accent␀␀m0␀␀m1␀␀morning␀Â£␀␀$␀␀␀â‚¬␀cur␀lo␀␀hi␀␀race␀␀␀␀wx␀␀place␀␀␀temp␀␀␀␀feels␀␀␀text␀␀␀␀rainHour␀␀␀␀rainPct␀wind␀␀␀␀handle␀␀subs␀␀␀␀step␀␀␀␀rate␀␀␀␀stepAt␀␀joined␀␀avatar␀␀statsOk␀d1␀␀d7␀␀d30␀histStart␀␀␀vw␀␀lv␀␀usual␀␀␀next␀␀␀␀prev␀␀␀␀vt␀␀ageMin␀␀typical␀at1h␀␀␀␀base1h␀␀at24h␀␀␀base24h␀cmp␀pts␀viewers␀thumb␀␀␀game␀␀␀␀mo␀␀lm␀␀pb␀␀dayT␀␀␀␀week␀␀␀␀weekT␀␀␀vidT␀␀␀␀vidTitle␀␀␀␀cmOff␀␀␀r